From c203dd50e1705ce3dd9211e3711190d3010b7950 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 15:29:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Uniform card heights and in-browser attribute editing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Layout: replace the CSS-columns masonry with a grid where every card is
the same height — one fixed picture box (--card-ratio) plus a fixed-height
body. Defaults to object-fit: contain so full-body outfits aren't cropped;
--card-fit: cover switches to a tighter, cropped grid.

Editing: Pages can't write files, so the lightbox gains an Edit form that
saves to localStorage and a bar that exports a regenerated data.json to
commit. The form is generated from each record, so invented attributes get
inputs automatically, and Add creates new text/list/group attributes.

Also fixes two bugs found while testing:
- the backdrop handler closed the dialog when a control re-rendered the
  panel mid-click, since the clicked node was detached by then; it now
  tests the backdrop element itself
- elements with an explicit display stayed painted while [hidden], which
  left the read-only detail list showing behind the edit form

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018L2BZgrSpCaQ8RPdasHPtR
